This changes `EllipsoidJoint`'s `radii_x_y_z` property to default to 1.0 in
each dimension, rather than NaN.

The NaN default means that loading an osim file that omits `radii_x_y_z`
propagates NaN into `MobilizedBody::Ellipsoid::setDefaultRadii`, which has a
Debug-only `assert(r[0]>0 && r[1]>0 && r[2]>0)`. Because every comparison
against NaN is false, the assertion fires and aborts the process, so such a
file loads in a Release build but crashes a Debug build.

OPynSim philosophy note: if a data file works in a release of OpenSim then
OPynSim should try to accept it: regardless of build configuration. A unit
radii default is also a more useful fallback than NaN, because the radii are
used for visualization: a NaN ellipsoid cannot be drawn, whereas a unit one
can.

---

diff --git a/OpenSim/Simulation/SimbodyEngine/EllipsoidJoint.cpp b/OpenSim/Simulation/SimbodyEngine/EllipsoidJoint.cpp
--- a/OpenSim/Simulation/SimbodyEngine/EllipsoidJoint.cpp
+++ b/OpenSim/Simulation/SimbodyEngine/EllipsoidJoint.cpp
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@
 void EllipsoidJoint::constructProperties()
 {
     setAuthors("Ajay Seth");
-    SimTK::Vec3 radii(NaN);
+    SimTK::Vec3 radii(1.0);
     constructProperty_radii_x_y_z(radii);
 
     Appearance appearance;
